1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Leo is at the airport.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
He's going on his first trip to London.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
But something is wrong. He doesn't know where to go!

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Oh no! Where is the check-in counter?

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Don't worry, Leo! I'll help you.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Leo and Emma walk into the airport.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Emma, I'm a little nervous.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
It's okay! Traveling is exciting. Just follow me.

9
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,000
What's the first thing we need to do?

10
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
We need to check in and get your boarding pass.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Good morning! Where are you flying today?

12
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
I'm flying to London.

13
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:44,000
May I see your passport, please?

14
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Of course. Here you are.

15
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Thank you. Do you have any bags to check in?

16
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Yes, I have one suitcase.

17
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Perfect. Here is your boarding pass.

18
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Thank you very much!

19
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Emma, where is Gate 12?

20
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Let's look at the information screen.

21
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Oh! It says Gate 12 is on the left.

22
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:51,000
That's right! Let's go.

23
00:02:51,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Thank you for helping me!

24
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Please put your bag on the tray.

25
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Okay. Is this everything?

26
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Yes. Please walk through the scanner.

27
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Leo passes the security check. Everything is fine!

28
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Attention, please! Passengers for London, boarding is now open.

29
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Emma! It's time to board!

30
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Yes! Have a wonderful trip!

31
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Thank you! See you soon!

32
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Leo smiles and walks toward the airplane.

33
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:30,000
He is ready for his first adventure!

34
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Great job! Now let's learn five useful English phrases from Leo's story.

35
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Where is the check-in counter?

36
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:59,000
May I see your passport?

37
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Here you are.

38
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Where is Gate 12?

39
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Have a wonderful trip!

40
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Listen and repeat. Where is Gate 12?

41
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:45,000
May I see your passport, please?

42
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Here you are.

43
00:05:53,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Let's take a quick quiz! What does “boarding pass” mean?

44
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:11,000
A) A passport.
B) A boarding document.
C) A suitcase.

45
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Pause the video and choose your answer!

46
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:29,000
B is correct! A boarding pass is the document you need to get on the plane. Well done!

47
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:43,000
If you enjoyed this story, subscribe to EnglishTale and learn English with us.

48
00:06:43,000 --> 00:07:00,000
See you in the next story!